language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_003_quasigroup_existence: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ An order m quasigroup is a Latin square of size m: an m-by-m multiplication table in which each element occurs once in every row and column, with the elements 0 to m-1. Find an order m quasigroup (the operation a * b) such that (a*b)*(b*a) = a for every a and b. This is the QG3.m quasigroup existence problem.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_003_quasigroup_existence.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_003_quasigroup_existence.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_003_quasigroup_existence_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_003_quasigroup_existence.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_003_quasigroup_existence_1.param -run-solver

$ m: the order of the quasigroup (the size of its table)
given m : int(1..)

$ quasigroup[i,j]: the value of i-1 * j-1 (table indices 1-based, values 0 to m-1, so the value v is at table index v+1)
find quasigroup : matrix indexed by [int(1..m), int(1..m)] of int(0..m-1)

such that
$ every row of the table has each element exactly once
forAll i : int(1..m) . allDiff(quasigroup[i,..]),
$ every column of the table has each element exactly once
forAll j : int(1..m) . allDiff(quasigroup[..,j]),
$ for every a and b, (a*b)*(b*a) = a
forAll a : int(0..m-1) . forAll b : int(0..m-1) . quasigroup[quasigroup[a+1,b+1]+1, quasigroup[b+1,a+1]+1] = a
